      "id": "",
      "title": "Depersonalization-derealization disorder",
      "url": "",
      "author": "BlockArranger",
      "summary": "A Depersonalization-derealization disorder (DPDR) is a dissociative mental disorder where a person experiences persistent or recurrent feelings of being detached from themselves (depersonalization) and/or from their surroundings (derealization). Common descriptions include feeling like an outside observer of one’s thoughts or body, or perceiving the world as foggy, dreamlike, or distorted. It is often linked to interpersonal trauma in childhood and stress or anxiety. Episodes can last from minutes to months, and in some cases longer. Diagnosis requires that these symptoms cause significant distress or impair functioning. Treatment typically involves psychotherapy, with prognosis usually positive. Prevalence is about 1–2% of the general population at some point in life.",
